      "id": "delaware-holidays",
      "sourceUrl": "https://delcode.delaware.gov/title1/c005/index.html",
      "title": "The legal holidays of Delaware (1 Del. C. § 501(a)) that `us-federal-holidays`\ndoes not already close: Good Friday, the Friday after Thanksgiving and the\nbiennial General Election day. FRCP 6(a)(6)(C) and FRCrimP 45(a)(6)(C)\nmake them legal holidays of the District of Delaware for a period counted\nforward only, so they are read as `forward_holidays` (core's\n`frcp6-delaware` and `frcrimp45-delaware`). The other § 501\ndays are federal holidays too, observed on the same days (§ 501(b) moves a\nSaturday holiday to Friday and a Sunday one to Monday, as § 6103(b)(1)\nand Executive Order 11582 do; the three days here are never on a\nweekend); Saturdays (§ 501(a)(11)) are closed by `weekend`.\n\nThe engine has no Easter or \"day after\" rule, so each day is listed with\n`once`, from May 2, 2011 (the earliest date a D. Del. package needs: the\ncriminal plan's 2011 amendment) to the end of 2050. The vendored text's\ncredits list no act after 83 Del. Laws, c. 257, of the 2021-2022 General\nAssembly, which only numbered § 501(a)'s list and added Juneteenth; and\nnone between 77 Del. Laws, c. 328 (2010) and 83 Del. Laws, c. 37 (2021),\nwhose § 1 reprints § 501(a) as it then stood with all three days\n(sources/de-code/83-del-laws-c-37.txt). So the three days were\nholidays throughout the span. A day before or after it is not closed, so\na last day on it is the earlier date, never a later one. The General\nElection is held on the federal election day of even years; the Title 15\nsection fixing it is not vendored. Not modeled: Return Day (§ 501(a)(13)), a\nholiday in Sussex County only and only after noon; the 2 floating\nholidays of § 501(e), which are leave for State employees, not days; and\ndays the Governor appoints, which no vendored source lists."
    }
